My trouble with wizards has been that I play a little too wombatty,
but getting a throne wish on the way down to Sokoban, for +2 SDSM,
helps ease the sting of most early ill-chosen fights =)

No particular luck with wishes beyond that, though, the one would be
it until the Castle; then there were three magic lamps in Gehennom,
all of 'em blessed. One of the lamps gave me a pet instead of a wish,
though, and another yielded an *angry* djinn. Some demons have no
gratitude! Anyway, after many bouts of summoning, sacrificing,
praying, and polypiling at an altar on DL6, I had everything but a
=oLev and decided it was time.

Kitty Three (a purple worm) and I had some fun with Rodney on the way
back up: "So, you thought you could -"
BUURRRRP!

The Planes were about as tricky than I was expecting (this is my
second ascension, but my first was as an extinctionist, so I hadn't
seen a populated Plane before) - but "charm 'em and run" worked out
fine except for Air, where I used up a few wands on the elementals,
and Astral, where I charmed but couldn't run without first clearning a
path with a /oTeleport. I tried the middle altar first, with Famine,
and whaddya know if it wasn't a lucky guess!

So there I was, standing on the altar with the amulet and my remaining
blessed magic lamp, and looking down at my shirt: "Madame Elvira's
House O' Succubi Employee of the Month". What better way to shake up
the heteronormativity of the Demi-Bar than by waltzing in with a wet
t-shirt (hadn't dried yet from the Plane of Water, natch) and a
succubus on my arm?

Spent the wish on a blessed figurine, which produced a peaceful
succubus who just wouldn't be tamed. Dang. Guess I could make a sort
of Dali-esque stage play on the squirming death and decay and
chitinous yuckitude inherent in all beings, even demideities; I
certainly ascended with enough pet bugs.

